---
/**
 * The shell every public route sits in. Plan 05-06, Tasks 1 and 2.
 *
 * Five requirements live here rather than in any route, which is why one defect in this file is
 * five broken routes: PUB-12 (no flash of the wrong theme), PUB-13 (reduced motion), PUB-11's
 * print MODE, SEO-01's landing place, and PUB-14's "zero framework JavaScript", which is a
 * property of the shell because the shell is what every route inherits.
 *
 * ================================================================================================
 * THE ONE CSS IMPORT, AND THE ONE SCRIPT
 * ================================================================================================
 *
 * `src/styles/design-system.css` is imported HERE and nowhere else in the repository (§1.2). It
 * holds the four design-system stylesheets in dependency order; a page that imported three of the
 * four would render with unthemed primitives and look merely "a bit off" rather than broken, which
 * is the kind of defect that ships.
 *
 * There is exactly ONE `<script>` on any public route and it is the `is:inline` block below
 * (§5.2). PUB-14 bans React hydration, not a hand-written script — but it bans a SECOND one, and
 * it bans any `client:*` directive outside `/photos`.
 *
 * ================================================================================================
 * WHY THE THEME SCRIPT EXISTS AT ALL — D-34, AND IT IS DELETABLE
 * ================================================================================================
 *
 * `@akhil-saxena/design-system@2.0.0-beta.1` SHIPS NO THEME ENTRY POINT. MEASURED: its exports map
 * is `.`, `./hooks`, `./icons`, `./components/*`, `./tokens.css`, `./primitives.css`,
 * `./utilities.css`, `./themes/*.css`, `./fonts/*.css`, `./css/*` — there is no `applyTheme`, no
 * `useTheme`, no `/theme`. D-34 was decided in DSGN-05 and Phase 1 did not ship it.
 *
 * DSGN-05's own reasoning is why this is a FINDING and not a preference: `.dark` and `data-brand`
 * are the DESIGN SYSTEM's selectors, changed on its release schedule, so leaving every consumer to
 * reinvent the script is how consumers drift out of sync with a contract they do not own. The
 * portfolio and Cairn would each carry a copy.
 *
 * OQ-3 resolves this as: write it locally AND file the gap upstream for `2.0.0-beta.2`. The Core
 * Value says a gap the design system exposes is a finding rather than a workaround; it does not say
 * the finding must be fixed before the consumer ships, and the live site is down, which is a clock.
 *
 * >>> DELETE THE SCRIPT BELOW, AND THIS COMMENT, THE DAY THE PACKAGE SHIPS A THEME ENTRY POINT. <<<
 *
 * ================================================================================================
 * THE CONTRACT THE SCRIPT MUST NOT BREAK
 * ================================================================================================
 *
 *  - `data-brand` and `class="dark"` are SERVER-RENDERED ATTRIBUTES on <html>, not script-set. A
 *    script that sets the brand paints one frame of the default brand first. In the markup they
 *    are in the cascade before the first byte of body is parsed.
 *  - DARK IS THE DEFAULT AND `prefers-color-scheme` IS NOT CONSULTED. `REQUIREMENTS.md` Out of
 *    Scope: "Three-state theme toggle — Two states, dark by default, as designed." The script's
 *    only theme job is to REMOVE `dark` for a returning light-mode visitor.
 *  - The `localStorage` read is wrapped in `try`. Safari in private mode throws on ACCESS, and an
 *    unhandled throw here aborts the script before the class is corrected — a flash caused by the
 *    code that exists to prevent one, on the one path nobody exercises by accident.
 *  - `beforeprint`/`afterprint` are OQ-5, and they restate NO TOKEN. `themes/monochrome.css`
 *    contains zero at-rules by design and CSS cannot remove a class, so this is the smallest
 *    correct mechanism and it works on every page rather than only on `/resume`.
 *    RESIDUAL, RECORDED NOT HIDDEN: some headless print-to-PDF paths do not fire `beforeprint`.
 *    That risk is accepted (OQ-5) and filed upstream as a request for a theme print block or a
 *    `data-force-light` hook.
 *  - PHASE 8: NO CSP IS CONFIGURED ON THIS SITE TODAY. If one is added, this script needs a hash
 *    or a nonce. Written here so it is a scheduled cost rather than a discovery at cutover.
 *
 * The listener is DELEGATED from `document` rather than bound to the button by
 * `DOMContentLoaded` + `getElementById`. The script runs in `<head>`, so the button does not exist
 * yet; delegation is live from that instant, needs no second lifecycle event, and cannot miss a
 * click landing between parse and `DOMContentLoaded`.
 *
 * ================================================================================================
 * WHAT IS NOT HERE
 * ================================================================================================
 *
 * No `<title>`, no `<meta name="description">`, no canonical, no `og:*`. Those are `<Seo>`'s, and
 * they arrive through the named `head` slot so that no page ever hand-writes a meta tag (SEO-01).
 * A layout that emitted a default title would give every route that forgot `<Seo>` a plausible
 * wrong one instead of a visibly missing one.
 */

import { Footer } from '@akhil-saxena/design-system/components/Footer';
import homeConfig from '../../data/home_config.json';
import { type PublicNavVariant, PublicNav } from '../components/public/PublicNav';
import '../styles/design-system.css';
import '../styles/public-shell.css';

interface Props {
  /** Extra class(es) for `<main>` — normally one of the `.pub-max-*` page maxima (§2.2). */
  mainClass?: string;
  /**
   * How the top row is drawn. `bar` (the default, 51 documents) is the design system's `AppBar`;
   * `plain` is Home's, which the approved design gives no bar at all — see `PublicNav.tsx`.
   *
   * It is a prop rather than a `pathname === '/'` test inside the layout because the shell must
   * not know which route is special. A layout that hard-coded the exception would make the second
   * page that wants a plain row an edit to a file shared by every page that does not.
   */
  navVariant?: PublicNavVariant;
}

const { mainClass, navVariant = 'bar' } = Astro.props;

/**
 * The footer's links are `data/home_config.json`'s `socialLinks`, mapped to `Footer`'s shape.
 *
 * `Footer.links` is PLAIN DATA (`Array<{ label, href }>`), not a `ReactNode`, so it crosses the
 * `.astro` → React boundary without the wrapper `PublicNav.tsx` needs. See that file's header for
 * the measurement of where the boundary actually is.
 *
 * 🔴 A MEASURED DEFECT SHIPS HERE, DELIBERATELY, AND IT IS FILED UPSTREAM.
 * §4.6b says "Phase 5 uses `variant='default'` in the footer, which is stylesheet-only and
 * therefore correct." THAT ESCAPE DOES NOT EXIST. `Footer`'s own `renderLink` hardcodes
 * `<Link variant="footer" className="ds-atom-footer-link">` (MEASURED, `chunk-23WQN7ZH.js.map`),
 * and `Footer` exposes no per-item className, style or variant hook — `className` reaches the
 * `<footer>` element only. So every consumer of `Footer.links` gets `variant="footer"`, whose
 * INLINE `textDecorationColor: rgba(0,0,0,.25)` beats the dark-mode stylesheet rule that would set
 * `rgba(255,255,255,.4)`. On `#0d0d0f` that underline is effectively invisible.
 *
 * NOT PATCHED LOCALLY. The only local fix is an `!important` reaching past a component into its
 * internals, which is the workaround the Core Value forbids and which Phase 0 declined for the
 * same class of defect (D-16-1). The link TEXT is `var(--ink)` and correct in both modes; only its
 * underline is wrong, so this degrades appearance rather than function. Filed for
 * `2.0.0-beta.2` — `Link`'s `footer`/`action` variants should move their colour and
 * decoration into `primitives.css` where the `.dark` rule can win.
 */
const footerLinks = homeConfig.socialLinks.map((link) => ({
  label: link.label,
  href: link.url,
}));

/**
 * DERIVED, never typed. The name comes from `home_config.json` (the same string the Home hero
 * uses) and the year from the build clock, so neither can go stale in a file nobody re-reads.
 * Evaluated during prerender, which runs in workerd — `Date` is available there; a filesystem read
 * would not be (05-01).
 */
const copyright = `© ${new Date().getFullYear()} ${homeConfig.title}`;
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" data-brand="monochrome" class="dark">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    {
      /* A real device-width viewport. The six-class responsive contract runs from a 344px folded
        cover screen to 1440px+, and there is no fixed pixel width anywhere in this file. A brace
        comment rather than an HTML one: an HTML comment SHIPS to every page, and this note is for
        the author. (Do not spell the delimiters out here — a nested terminator ends the comment
        early and the compiler reports only "Unexpected token" at the line after.) */
    }
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
    <script is:inline>
      /* D-34 · the design system ships no theme entry point at 2.0.0-beta.1, so this is a local
         copy of a selector contract this repository does not own. Filed upstream for
         2.0.0-beta.2; delete it the day `@akhil-saxena/design-system/theme` exists.
         Phase 8: no CSP today — adding one requires a hash or a nonce for this block.
         Full rationale, and the residual on headless print, in this file's frontmatter. */
      (function () {
        var d = document.documentElement;
        var s = null;
        try {
          s = localStorage.getItem('theme');
        } catch (e) {
          /* Safari private mode throws on access. Falling through leaves the default dark. */
        }
        if (s === 'light') d.classList.remove('dark');
        addEventListener('beforeprint', function () {
          d.classList.remove('dark');
        });
        addEventListener('afterprint', function () {
          if (s !== 'light') d.classList.add('dark');
        });
        document.addEventListener('click', function (ev) {
          var t = ev.target;
          if (!t || !t.closest || !t.closest('#pub-theme-toggle')) return;
          s = d.classList.toggle('dark') ? 'dark' : 'light';
          try {
            localStorage.setItem('theme', s);
          } catch (e) {
            /* Storage denied: the class still flipped, the choice just will not survive a reload. */
          }
        });
      })();
    </script>
    <slot name="head" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <div class="pub-shell">
      <div class={navVariant === 'plain' ? 'pub-bar pub-bar-plain' : 'pub-bar'}>
        <PublicNav
          siteTitle={homeConfig.title}
          pathname={Astro.url.pathname}
          variant={navVariant}
        />
      </div>
      <main class={mainClass ? `pub-main ${mainClass}` : 'pub-main'}>
        <slot />
      </main>
      <div class="pub-footer">
        <Footer variant="compact" copyright={copyright} links={footerLinks} />
      </div>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
